{
	"_comment": [
		"Pinned, hash-verified FFmpeg/FFprobe binaries. Read scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.mjs first.",
		"",
		"Every URL here is an immutable, versioned address -- never a 'latest' redirect --",
		"so a build made today and a build made next year fetch the identical bytes.",
		"",
		"Two builders, chosen per platform rather than per vendor, because LICENSING VARIES",
		"BY PLATFORM WITHIN A SINGLE BUILDER. martin-riedl's macOS builds are clean GPL but",
		"its Linux builds set --enable-nonfree; BtbN ships no macOS at all. That is why the",
		"fetch script re-verifies the configure line of every binary it extracts instead of",
		"trusting the source. Do not 'simplify' this to one builder without re-verifying.",
		"",
		"To bump: change the URLs, run `node scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.mjs --print-hashes` for",
		"each target, paste the hashes back here, and update THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md section 2.",
		"",
		"A 404 from a BtbN URL means the release was PRUNED, not that the script broke: BtbN",
		"keeps daily autobuilds for only ~2 weeks, but keeps each month's LAST autobuild",
		"(autobuild-YYYY-MM-<last day>-*) long-term. Pin a month-end tag; list them with",
		"`gh release list --repo BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds`."
	],

